[
  {
    "id": "dashboard_flow_tab",
    "type": "tab",
    "label": "ESP32 MMDVM - Dashboard",
    "disabled": false,
    "info": "# ESP32 MMDVM Hotspot - Monitoring Dashboard\n\nThis flow creates a complete monitoring dashboard with real-time updates.\n\n## Prerequisites:\n\n**Install node-red-dashboard:**\n```\ncd ~/.node-red\nnpm install node-red-dashboard\n```\n\nRestart Node-RED after installation.\n\n## Quick Start:\n\n1. **Update Base URL & Credentials (if needed):**\n   - Edit the change node labeled \"Set Base URL & Auth\"\n   - Default URL: http://esp32-mmdvm.local\n   - Default credentials: admin / pi-star\n   - Update the URL in the first rule if your ESP32 has a different address\n   - Update the credentials in the JSONata expression if different: $base64encode(\"admin:pi-star\")\n\n3. **Access the Dashboard:**\n   - Navigate to `http://your-node-red-ip:1880/ui`\n   - The dashboard will show:\n     - System metrics (CPU, memory, uptime)\n     - DMR activity status\n     - Network status\n     - Modem information\n\n## Dashboard Features:\n\n- **Auto-refresh** every 5 seconds\n- **Memory usage gauge** with threshold alerts\n- **Uptime display** in human-readable format\n- **DMR activity** real-time display\n- **Network status** indicators\n- **Charts** for memory usage over time\n\n## Customization:\n\nYou can adjust:\n- Refresh interval (change the inject node repeat value)\n- Gauge thresholds (edit gauge node settings)\n- Chart history length (edit chart node buffer size)"
  },
  {
    "id": "dashboard_ui_tab",
    "type": "ui_tab",
    "name": "ESP32 MMDVM Monitor",
    "icon": "dashboard",
    "order": 1,
    "disabled": false,
    "hidden": false
  },
  {
    "id": "dashboard_group_system",
    "type": "ui_group",
    "name": "System Status",
    "tab": "dashboard_ui_tab",
    "order": 1,
    "disp": true,
    "width": "6",
    "collapse": false
  },
  {
    "id": "dashboard_group_dmr",
    "type": "ui_group",
    "name": "DMR Activity",
